cpp-pinyin
------------------------------------------
cpp-pinyin is a lightweight Chinese/Cantonese to Pinyin library.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libcpp-pinyin2-devel-2.0.0-1bl1
  libcpp-pinyin2_2-2.0.0-1bl1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  git-2.51.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  python3-3.12.12-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/wolfgitpr/cpp-pinyin

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/wolfgitpr/cpp-pinyin/archive/refs/tags/v2.0.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack cpp-pinyin-2.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./cpp-pinyin-2.0.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/cpp-pinyin-2.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/cpp-pinyin-2.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcpp-pinyin2_2-2.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcpp-pinyin2-devel-2.0.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

